# Muse Game Workshop

Read and follow @AGENTS.md as the authoritative repository rule file. Read @CLAUDE.md as a thin tool-adapter summary and use @README.md as the product entry point.

Before modifying code, assets, skills, templates, examples, or project structure:

1. State the production stage.
2. Provide a design summary, execution plan, impact scope, file list, review decisions, and validation plan.
3. Wait for `Approved`.
4. Stop on `Needs revision` or `Rejected`.

The canonical workflow skills live under `.agents/skills/`. Read the matching `SKILL.md` completely before acting. Cursor rules and commands are adapters only; they must not fork the workflow core, bypass evidence requirements, or change production stages and terminology.

Keep engine-neutral design truth separate from Three.js, Unity, Unreal, and Godot mappings. Preserve unrelated changes and run the smallest relevant checks under `tools/checks/` after approved work.
